{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>These are the sons of Seir, etc.</b> The reason for making this matter known is to inform us of the measure of what HaShem gave, in the merit of the fathers, to Esau even though he was wicked. And our Sages of blessed memory also expounded this in tractate Shabbat, chapter Rabbi Akiva (Shabbat 85a), and this is their language: Rabbi Aḥa bar Ya'akov said, Ḥori — because they became free men (benei ḥorin) from their property — end of quote. You see that Scripture recounts their having been given to Esau. And they further said (Sanhedrin 99b) that it is to inform us about Timna — that she was at the height of the ranks, sister of Lotan, yet became a concubine to Eliphaz. Both these and those are words of the living Elohim."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:46:15.346590495Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}